1
00:00:01,158 --> 00:00:03,090
Claws, Wings, and Fangs

2
00:00:04,179 --> 00:00:06,705
Well? Any luck finding Blaion?

3
00:00:06,705 --> 00:00:09,640
It's no use. No matter how hard I look, I can't find them.

4
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:11,374
And it doesn't help that the footage is so dark at night...

5
00:00:11,374 --> 00:00:15,782
I haven't seen any posts on social media mentioning a suspicious looking fire truck, either.

6
00:00:18,064 --> 00:00:19,911
Phantom Hornet, Sealed.

7
00:00:19,911 --> 00:00:21,465
Soleil...?

8
00:00:21,465 --> 00:00:23,564
I'll be taking her with me.

9
00:00:23,564 --> 00:00:24,149
You...!

10
00:00:24,149 --> 00:00:25,106
Wait!

11
00:00:25,106 --> 00:00:26,185
Don't follow us!

12
00:00:26,362 --> 00:00:27,631
Aah!

13
00:00:28,142 --> 00:00:29,244
F-Fire!!

14
00:00:32,785 --> 00:00:33,440
Are you okay?

15
00:00:34,434 --> 00:00:37,636
(At the time, I was so shocked that I couldn't do anything.)

16
00:00:37,636 --> 00:00:39,886
Soleil had a Metal Breath.

17
00:00:39,886 --> 00:00:43,135
If she's carrying Blaion around sealed in card form, it'll be impossible to find them.

18
00:00:43,135 --> 00:00:44,995
I suppose that's true...

19
00:00:44,995 --> 00:00:48,616
Ugh... Is there any way I can find Soleil again?

20
00:00:48,616 --> 00:00:51,372
Would things get too complicated if we asked the police for help?

21
00:00:51,372 --> 00:00:55,657
We can't use the public safety radio again. My dad really scolded me for that.

22
00:00:55,657 --> 00:00:57,274
Sorry about that...

23
00:00:57,274 --> 00:00:59,221
Come to think of it, you're the daughter of the mayor, Anna.

24
00:00:59,221 --> 00:01:01,122
Yes, I am. Why?

25
00:01:01,122 --> 00:01:02,600
Tell the mayor:

26
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:05,478
We need to put the entire city of Mowtown under lockdown immediately!

27
00:01:05,978 --> 00:01:07,142
WHAAAAA?!

28
00:01:07,142 --> 00:01:08,662
What do you mean by that, Mega Ambler?

29
00:01:08,662 --> 00:01:10,101
Why a lockdown all of a sudden?

30
00:01:10,101 --> 00:01:14,226
What do you mean, all of a sudden?! After Phantom Hornet was sealed by that kid, they've gone missing!

31
00:01:14,226 --> 00:01:17,556
If they start spreading the Beast Virus indiscriminately, it’ll be the end of us—

32
00:01:17,556 --> 00:01:20,087
and the end of our coexistence with humans, too!

33
00:01:20,087 --> 00:01:23,862
When the infected Metal Cardbots go on a rampage, the only outcome is total annihilation...!

34
00:01:23,862 --> 00:01:25,343
T-That sounds really bad...

35
00:01:25,343 --> 00:01:28,690
Soleil wouldn't do something like spreading the virus.

36
00:01:28,690 --> 00:01:30,196
How can you be so sure?

37
00:01:30,196 --> 00:01:35,642
She fixed Blue Cop! If she were to go around spreading the virus, she wouldn't have helped us out in the first place!

38
00:01:35,642 --> 00:01:39,217
You’re too naive. She's on the Wild Cardbots' side, after all.

39
00:01:39,217 --> 00:01:42,260
She'll put us in danger with all kinds of lies and deception, just like those Wild Cardbots do!

40
00:01:42,260 --> 00:01:43,111
You're overreacting...!

41
00:01:43,111 --> 00:01:46,839
Then why did she steal your chance to seal a Wild Cardbot and run away?! Answer me!

42
00:01:46,839 --> 00:01:48,042
How should I know that?!

43
00:01:48,042 --> 00:01:49,779
Enough! Calm down, both of you!

44
00:01:49,779 --> 00:01:52,952
Now, now, let's think this through one step at a time, guys.

45
00:01:54,152 --> 00:01:55,566
I'm sorry for yelling.

46
00:01:55,566 --> 00:01:58,829
It's... it's okay. I'm sorry, too.

47
00:01:59,093 --> 00:02:02,703
First, I'll tell my colleagues about the Wild Cardbots...

48
00:02:02,703 --> 00:02:06,112
and that another owner of the Metal Breath has appeared.

49
00:02:06,912 --> 00:02:09,180
Good. I'll leave it to you.

50
00:02:12,032 --> 00:02:15,198
Ugh. Lockdown? There's no way we can do that.

51
00:02:15,198 --> 00:02:18,104
I've never seen Mega Ambler so upset...

52
00:02:18,104 --> 00:02:22,878
He's a doctor, after all. He's seen many lives lost to Wild Cardbots.

53
00:02:22,878 --> 00:02:24,851
Please be understanding, even if he acts a little sensitive.

54
00:02:24,851 --> 00:02:28,719
I thought planet Machina was peaceful until its lifespan came to an end...

55
00:02:28,719 --> 00:02:32,297
I guess even a distant planet isn't all that different from Earth.

56
00:02:34,097 --> 00:02:36,533
Huh? Uncle! Wait up!

57
00:02:36,533 --> 00:02:39,354
What? What? Hey, hey! That was in the trash!

58
00:02:39,354 --> 00:02:42,069
I've got an idea... I know how to find Soleil!

59
00:02:42,769 --> 00:02:44,835
You want me to publish an article about a missing person?

60
00:02:44,835 --> 00:02:46,977
A girl named Soleil has gone missing!

61
00:02:46,977 --> 00:02:49,044
We need to find her as soon as possible!

62
00:02:49,044 --> 00:02:52,223
I can't! I don't have the power to do something like that!

63
00:02:52,223 --> 00:02:56,509
Hey, why are you being such a stranger? We're partners who saved the world together!

64
00:02:56,509 --> 00:03:02,535
Not to mention the photos you took in Porcaca played a crucial role in the coexistence of humans and Metal Cardbots!

65
00:03:02,535 --> 00:03:05,579
Please, Mister Hawkins. Our society of coexistence is under threat.

66
00:03:05,579 --> 00:03:11,733
Well... I do owe you guys for everything. And I really do want to help you guys out, but...

67
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:14,847
Why are you stalling over there, Jim?! Hurry on over there before it gets away!

68
00:03:14,847 --> 00:03:15,869
Y-yes, sir!!

69
00:03:16,369 --> 00:03:18,453
And you. Don't disturb the adults while they're working.

70
00:03:18,453 --> 00:03:20,019
Ehehehe... What's going on, anyway?

71
00:03:20,019 --> 00:03:22,415
An octopus monster appeared at Landfill No. 30!

72
00:03:22,415 --> 00:03:23,413
An octopus?!

73
00:03:23,513 --> 00:03:26,501
We’re here at the bridge construction site at Landfill No. 30.

74
00:03:26,501 --> 00:03:32,688
Reports are pouring in that a giant octopus monster was spotted here this morning, prompting citizens to remain on high alert.

75
00:03:32,688 --> 00:03:36,437
Could this be related to the unidentified Metal Cardbots that caused a commotion recently?

76
00:03:36,437 --> 00:03:38,643
Oh! There! I saw something!

77
00:03:39,943 --> 00:03:41,609
Well? Do you see anything?

78
00:03:41,909 --> 00:03:44,943
Hmmm... Oh!

79
00:03:45,317 --> 00:03:48,349
I got it! But that's not an octopus. That's a tank!

80
00:03:48,349 --> 00:03:49,463
A tank?!

81
00:03:49,463 --> 00:03:52,398
A tank standing alone in a landfill rich in methane gas...

82
00:03:52,398 --> 00:03:55,733
It's only natural to assume that it's a Metal Cardbot that has come to collect energy.

83
00:03:55,733 --> 00:03:58,921
So that Metal Cardbot is a stranger to you guys, right?

84
00:03:58,921 --> 00:03:59,717
Eh?

85
00:04:02,525 --> 00:04:04,267
Aaaahh!!

86
00:04:05,825 --> 00:04:06,472
Jun!

87
00:04:09,283 --> 00:04:12,687
What's going on?! I thought Metal Cardbots were friends with humans now!

88
00:04:12,687 --> 00:04:14,585
I don't think that's a Metal Cardbot, but a...

89
00:04:16,358 --> 00:04:18,156
We have no choice. Let's head to the landfill!

90
00:04:18,156 --> 00:04:18,774
Alright!

91
00:04:19,818 --> 00:04:20,656
You guys get out of here!

92
00:04:20,656 --> 00:04:21,391
Jun!

93
00:04:27,995 --> 00:04:29,250
Incoming!

94
00:04:29,250 --> 00:04:30,162
Hold on tight!

95
00:04:39,445 --> 00:04:40,159
Where are they?

96
00:04:40,159 --> 00:04:41,345
Be careful, Blue Cop.

97
00:04:43,708 --> 00:04:44,788
ROAR!!!

98
00:04:54,959 --> 00:04:57,679
Yahahahaha!

99
00:05:00,020 --> 00:05:01,753
You're a Metal Cardbot, right?

100
00:05:01,753 --> 00:05:03,493
Blue Cop! Reverse! Reverse!!

101
00:05:03,493 --> 00:05:04,210
I'm on it!

102
00:05:13,075 --> 00:05:14,066
Who are you?!

103
00:05:14,066 --> 00:05:17,085
Grrrhahaha! The name is Tigun!

104
00:05:20,277 --> 00:05:24,626
The strongest Wild Cardbot on planet Machina, if I do say so myself! Grrrhahaha! 

105
00:05:24,626 --> 00:05:25,664
Of course.

106
00:05:25,664 --> 00:05:28,314
Ugh... another one of those "I'm the strongest!" guys.

107
00:05:28,314 --> 00:05:29,236
Huh? Whatcha' say?!

108
00:05:29,236 --> 00:05:31,974
Planet Machina disappeared a long time ago.

109
00:05:31,974 --> 00:05:37,913
That title doesn’t mean anything here, so wouldn’t it be better for you to find a new identity here on Earth?

110
00:05:37,913 --> 00:05:40,311
And besides, there are plenty of others who are stronger than you, y'hear?!

111
00:05:40,311 --> 00:05:41,174
And there are worse ones, too!

112
00:05:41,174 --> 00:05:42,168
Who are we talking about??

113
00:05:42,914 --> 00:05:48,330
Grrrhahaha! You've got some guts to preach to me like that!

114
00:05:48,330 --> 00:05:50,945
There's no way we can talk him down, can we?

115
00:05:50,945 --> 00:05:51,880
I wasn't even counting on it.

116
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:54,523
Blue Cop Wild! Set Up!

117
00:06:05,373 --> 00:06:06,888
Roar!

118
00:06:07,988 --> 00:06:08,865
Burst Gun!

119
00:06:16,647 --> 00:06:18,331
Sniff Sniff. Eh?!

120
00:06:18,331 --> 00:06:21,816
You a Wild Cardbot or a Metal Cardbot? Which side are ya on?!

121
00:06:21,816 --> 00:06:25,201
Jun told me... that kind of thing doesn't matter here!

122
00:06:26,601 --> 00:06:29,523
I am Blue Cop! A resident of Earth!

123
00:06:29,523 --> 00:06:31,147
The heck you sayin'?!

124
00:06:32,647 --> 00:06:34,437
Mega Ambler! Phoenix Fire!

125
00:06:34,437 --> 00:06:35,396
Where's Blue Cop?

126
00:06:35,396 --> 00:06:37,439
They're across the bridge, fighting against a tank.

127
00:06:37,439 --> 00:06:38,401
A tank??

128
00:06:38,401 --> 00:06:40,087
Could this be another Wild Cardbot?

129
00:06:40,087 --> 00:06:41,452
A Wild Cardbot? 

130
00:06:43,149 --> 00:06:45,314
Here comes Fleta Z... or not.

131
00:06:45,814 --> 00:06:47,399
I have a bad feeling about this.

132
00:06:49,727 --> 00:06:53,551
If you want to live on this planet, you must respect the lifeforms here!

133
00:06:53,551 --> 00:06:55,775
Everyone will accept you if you do that!

134
00:06:55,775 --> 00:07:01,315
I don't care 'bout any of that. A lone beast like me doesn't need a pack!

135
00:07:06,035 --> 00:07:07,623
Impressive...

136
00:07:07,623 --> 00:07:11,882
If you’re willing to respect others, you can stay with us, too!

137
00:07:11,882 --> 00:07:14,300
Don't make me laugh! Who told you I'd want that?!

138
00:07:30,337 --> 00:07:31,161
Now what?!

139
00:07:31,161 --> 00:07:35,301
You gentlemen look like you're having quite a lot of fun. May I join in too?

140
00:07:35,301 --> 00:07:36,635
When did you call your ally?

141
00:07:36,635 --> 00:07:38,605
What?! I don't know this guy!

142
00:07:38,605 --> 00:07:42,881
It's only a natural instinct for us to be drawn to the scent of battle, isn't it?

143
00:07:42,881 --> 00:07:44,521
Blue Cop! Wolf Howl Shot!!

144
00:07:49,973 --> 00:07:52,152
Who the heck is that guy?

145
00:07:55,718 --> 00:07:57,799
He looks just like Sky Gallop.

146
00:07:57,799 --> 00:07:59,889
Shall we have some delightful fun?

147
00:07:59,889 --> 00:08:01,480
Alpha Bolt Cannon!

148
00:08:16,575 --> 00:08:17,341
Blue Cop!

149
00:08:21,985 --> 00:08:23,290
Are you okay?!

150
00:08:23,290 --> 00:08:24,508
A wound like this is nothing...!

151
00:08:24,508 --> 00:08:33,071
Hmmm... Well, isn’t that strange? I imbued my Crimson Lance with the Beast Virus... yet you show no reaction to it at all?

152
00:08:33,071 --> 00:08:37,870
Ah. I can sense the aura of a raging beast lurking behind that kind face.

153
00:08:37,870 --> 00:08:40,887
You're a Wild Cardbot too, right? Why are you doing this?!

154
00:08:40,887 --> 00:08:44,690
Heh heh... All I will say is that my name is Night Griffon!

155
00:08:48,496 --> 00:08:51,454
Well, well, I can't say that your aim is particularly elegant.

156
00:08:51,454 --> 00:08:54,413
May I suggest you distinguish between enemies and allies when aiming?

157
00:08:54,413 --> 00:08:59,880
Grrrha! I don't care 'bout that. I'm just following my instinct to fight!

158
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:02,598
Blue Cop, let's retreat for now. Things are looking bad.

159
00:09:02,598 --> 00:09:03,530
Roger that, Jun!

160
00:09:06,723 --> 00:09:09,356
There is no way I'll let you gentlemen get away!

161
00:09:09,356 --> 00:09:12,172
Roar! Get back here!

162
00:09:15,161 --> 00:09:17,471
Huh? Oh! It's Blue Cop!

163
00:09:18,836 --> 00:09:19,542
Is that...?!

164
00:09:19,542 --> 00:09:21,021
Everyone get off of the bridge!

165
00:09:21,021 --> 00:09:23,598
Now, time for you to stop running away!

166
00:09:29,782 --> 00:09:30,498
What was that?!

167
00:09:34,378 --> 00:09:35,372
Deep Bite!

168
00:09:35,672 --> 00:09:39,378
CAAAAAAAAW!!! GET IT OOOOOFF!!! OW!! OW!!!

169
00:09:40,878 --> 00:09:43,818
Blegh. This chicken leg has no taste!

170
00:09:43,818 --> 00:09:45,091
Excuse me?!

171
00:09:46,755 --> 00:09:48,022
Cielo! Set Up!

172
00:09:48,022 --> 00:09:49,798
Whoopsie daisy. Watch your head!

173
00:09:53,266 --> 00:09:54,796
Deep Bite! Set Up!

174
00:09:57,990 --> 00:10:00,388
Huh? We have more challengers?

175
00:10:00,388 --> 00:10:03,356
Trident... Submarine!

176
00:10:08,294 --> 00:10:09,334
Roar!!

177
00:10:12,728 --> 00:10:16,124
Well now, looks like he's no ordinary interloper.

178
00:10:16,124 --> 00:10:19,621
Heh. My excitement has worn off. Until next time!

179
00:10:20,721 --> 00:10:23,299
Hah! I'll turn you into a wild fried chicken if you come back!

180
00:10:23,299 --> 00:10:24,590
Deep Bite!

181
00:10:24,590 --> 00:10:25,411
Yo!

182
00:10:25,411 --> 00:10:26,935
Peruru! Cielo!

183
00:10:26,935 --> 00:10:27,987
Good to see ya, Jun.

184
00:10:27,987 --> 00:10:29,965
That was pretty good timing on our part, wasn't it?

185
00:10:29,965 --> 00:10:31,743
All thanks to me.

186
00:10:32,743 --> 00:10:35,101
Blue Cop, it looks like you've lost a little weight since I last saw you.

187
00:10:35,101 --> 00:10:37,230
Ahaha... I went on a diet.

188
00:10:37,230 --> 00:10:38,958
By the way, when did you guys come to Mowtown?

189
00:10:39,158 --> 00:10:40,001
I called them here.

190
00:10:40,001 --> 00:10:41,211
Crest!

191
00:10:41,211 --> 00:10:43,642
Hey... you could've told me first, Crest.

192
00:10:43,642 --> 00:10:46,670
Sorry. I've been too busy looking into a few things.

193
00:10:46,670 --> 00:10:50,298
I need to talk to you with Deep Bite about the Wild Cardbots.

194
00:10:51,998 --> 00:10:55,605
Grr! Dang it, I can't fire my cannon because it's sopping wet!

195
00:10:55,605 --> 00:10:58,811
I'll be back after I fill my belly! Grrrhahaha!

196
00:11:18,472 --> 00:11:20,553
What do you think? Does this help?

197
00:11:20,553 --> 00:11:25,349
Of course it does. I can now create a vaccine, and it's all because of the sample you brought me.

198
00:11:25,349 --> 00:11:27,804
Thank you, Soleil. You're such a good girl.

199
00:11:27,804 --> 00:11:33,036
If you need anything else, just let me know. I'll do anything you ask, mother.

